{"name":"Wild Honey","hex":"#eecc00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Untamed; not domesticated.","Especially, being of the wild type: being of an unbroken ancestral line of undomesticated animals, as opposed to being feral, being an undomesticated animal whose ancestors were domesticated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Inaccurately; not on target.","Intended to be synchronized with film or video but recorded separately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild"},{"term":"honey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet, viscous, gold-colored fluid produced from plant nectar by bees, and often consumed by humans.","A variety of this substance."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Involving or resembling honey.","Of a pale yellow to brownish-yellow color, like most types of honey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wild Honey (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Wild Honey is a 1984 adaptation by British playwright Michael Frayn of an earlier play by Anton Chekhov. The original work, a sprawling five-hour drama from Chekhov's earliest years as a writer, has no title, but is usually known in English as Platonov, after its principal character \"Mikhail Platonov\", a disillusioned provincial schoolmaster."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Honey_(play)","wikidata":"Q8000660"},{"title":"Wild Honey (1918 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wild Honey is a 1918 silent film western directed by Francis J. Grandon and starring Doris Kenyon. The film is preserved in the archives of the Museum of Modern Art."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Wild_Honey_%281918%29_-_Ad_2.jpg/330px-Wild_Honey_%281918%29_-_Ad_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Honey_(1918_film)","wikidata":"Q18709165"},{"title":"Wild Honey (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Wild Honey is the thirteenth studio album by the American rock band the Beach Boys, released on December 18, 1967, by Capitol Records. Recorded between September and November, it was the group's first foray into soul music, influenced by the R&B of Motown and Stax Records, and their second album to credit production collectively to the band. It continued the lo-fi style of Smiley Smile."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Wild_honey_beach_boys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Honey_(album)","wikidata":"Q1051233"},{"title":"Honey","blocks":[{"text":"Honey is a sweet and viscous substance made by several species of bees, the best-known of which are honey bees. Honey is made and stored to nourish bee colonies. Bees produce honey by gathering and then refining the sugary secretions of plants or the secretions of other insects, like the honeydew of aphids. This refinement takes place both within individual bees, through regurgitation and enzymatic activity, and during storage in the hive, through water evaporation that concentrates the honey's sugars until it is thick and viscous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Runny_hunny.jpg/330px-Runny_hunny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey","wikidata":"Q10987"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Beach_Boys_1967_%28cropped_and_restored%29.jpg/500px-Beach_Boys_1967_%28cropped_and_restored%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Beach_Boys_1967_%28cropped_and_restored%29.jpg/1280px-Beach_Boys_1967_%28cropped_and_restored%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm